From: Androlinzberg maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] libhidl: answer an absent hwbinder device as a HIDL-less device

A hosted session has no /dev/hwbinder. Stock libhidl returns no service
manager in that case, which devices never reach for clients such as
keystore2's HAL-name lookup. When no hwservicemanager is installed, answer as
Android does on a device without HIDL support: NoHwServiceManager, with no
services and no registrations.

diff --git a/transport/ServiceManagement.cpp b/transport/ServiceManagement.cpp
index 447701f..81ea890 100644
--- a/transport/ServiceManagement.cpp
+++ b/transport/ServiceManagement.cpp
@@ -363,6 +363,12 @@ sp<IServiceManager1_2> defaultServiceManager1_2() {
         }
 
         if (access("/dev/hwbinder", F_OK|R_OK|W_OK) != 0) {
+            // A hosted session has no hwbinder device. Without an installed
+            // hwservicemanager it answers as a device without HIDL support.
+            if (!isHidlSupported()) {
+                gDefaultServiceManager = sp<NoHwServiceManager>::make();
+                return gDefaultServiceManager;
+            }
             // HwBinder not available on this device or not accessible to
             // this process.
             return nullptr;
